    rdfs:label "MS. Sale 67a" ;
    dct:date "1032",
        "1623" ;
    dct:description """The second half of Süheyli Efendi active
                                17th century 's history of Egypt, beginning with Selim
                                I, Sultan of the Turks, 1470-1520 's war with the Mamluk
                            sultans Qānṣūh al-Ghūrī, Sultan of Egypt and Syria,
                                -1516 and Ṭūman Bāy, Mamlūk Sulṭān,
                                active 1516-1517 and ending with the governorship of the
                            Ottoman Ḳara
                                Dāmād Muṣṭafā Paşa, -1628 . According to Ethé (1930: 1171)
                            a large portion of this work folio 5a
                                onwards is a direct translation of Ibn Zunbul, Aḥmad ibn ʻAlī,
                                active 16th century 's Arabic work تأریخ وقعة
                                الغوري Ta'rīkh waqʿat
                            al-Ghūrī .""" ;
    dct:identifier "manuscript_1708" ;
    dct:language "ota" ;
    dct:type "codex" ;
